  "question": {
    "text": "The role of depressants in &#39;Froth Floation method&#39; is to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Ra3EH",
      "text": "selectively prevent one component of the ore from coming to the froth.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MZ2IN",
      "text": "reduce the consumption of oil for froth formation.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "UICga",
      "text": "stabilize the froth.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "at1l5",
      "text": "enhance non-wettability of the mineral particles.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the froth floatation process, the role of the depressants is to separate two sulphide ores by selectively preventing one ore from forming froth.</p><p>For example, to separate two sulphide ores, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PbS</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnS</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>NaCN</mi></math> is utilised. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi></math> forms a combination with zinc on the surface of zinc sulphide, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>, preventing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnS</mi></math> from foaming selectively.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>NaCN</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ZnS</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
